{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Perhaps I will be able to strike them.</b> A term of striking. And do not wonder that it is in plural form, for we find its like: ״משכני אחריך נרוצה״ (draw me after you, we will run). Another interpretation: <b>I will strike them</b> — I and you: I in war and you in curse. And we find curse as a term of striking: ״נכנו בלשון״ (we were struck with the tongue)." "<b>And I will drive them out of the land.</b> Which they took from the hand of Sihon — for it was originally mine, when Sihon took it from the hand of the first king of Moab."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:13.505058266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}